    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <h3>How do I log a meal?</h3>
    <p>Tap the + button on the Today screen and choose Take Photo, From Gallery, Describe Food or Manual.</p>

    <h3>How accurate is the AI meal scan?</h3>
    <p>AI results are estimates. You can adjust portions and edit every item before saving.</p>

    <h3>How do I cancel my subscription?</h3>
    <p><strong>iPhone / iPad:</strong> Settings app → tap your name → Subscriptions → Nourix → Cancel Subscription.<br>
    <strong>Android:</strong> Google Play → Payments &amp; subscriptions → Subscriptions → Nourix → Cancel.</p>

    <h3>How do I get a refund?</h3>
    <p><strong>iPhone / iPad:</strong> refunds are handled by Apple at <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" target="_blank">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.<br>
    <strong>Android:</strong> contact <a href="https://support.google.com/googleplay" target="_blank">Google Play support</a>.</p>

    <h3>I subscribed but the app still shows Free.</h3>
    <p>Open Settings → Upgrade to Premium → Restore Purchases, using the same Apple ID / Google account you subscribed with.</p>

    <h3>How do I delete my account?</h3>
    <p>In the app: Settings → Delete Account. All your data is permanently deleted. Deleting your account does not cancel a subscription — cancel it as shown above.</p>

    <h3>Is Nourix medical advice?</h3>
    <p>No. Nourix is a general nutrition tracking app, not a medical device. Consult a healthcare professional before making significant changes to your diet.</p>

